I like the fact that Nethack provides you with the opportunity
to screw yourself over if you take certain actions that you're
not necessarily ready for.  Another example is quaffing a fountain
when you can't handle the resultant water moccasins or foocubus
dancing when you have low INT/CHA and no way to repair the
damage.  If you wait until it's safe, then no problem.  If you
can't wait or you don't know any better then you hurt yourself.
That adds texture and challenge to the game that would be lacking
if every action had built-in training wheels. YMMV, of course.

I also like the fact that some of the banes are pretty near
useless.  An experienced player can learn that some artifacts
are better than others, and just because a particular weapon
was a gift, doesn't necessarily mean that it's the BEST GIFT
EVAR.  If all the banes were equally powerful (or powerful
in different ways) then another opportunity to learn would
be removed.  Basically, it comes down to whether you think
Nethack is too hard already or not.  I don't, personally, but
I certainly respect your opinion if you think it is.

